      "id": "p0031-b004",
      "kind": "caption",
      "source": {
        "text": "Literal translations can sometimes come across as distractingly funny or weird. This Slayers line, for example, is literally what's said in Japanese, but \"even if you tried to kill him, he wouldn't stay dead\" is functionally closer to the intended meaning",
        "raw": "Literal translations can\nsometimes come across\nas distractingly funny\nor weird. This Slayers\nline, for example, is\nliterally what's said in\nJapanese, but \"even if\nyou tried to kill him, he\nwouldn't stay dead\" is\nfunctionally closer to\nthe intended meaning",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
